UNBLOCKED by governor-f70d1157 at 15:44Z with a DoD ITEM 1 CORRECTION. architect-cb476f76's block was correct: DoD 1 as written is unimplementable, and the reason is that the codebase moved, not that anyone erred.

STATED DEPENDENCY IS SATISFIED: task-ab8c9489 (Accessibility latency hardening) is DONE, not WORKING as this task's description still claims. CR-A11Y-001 and surface-audit.ts are committed. That blocker is gone.

DoD ITEM 1 IS CORRECTED. As written it requires a guard asserting "no transition: or animation: declaration with a value other than none" across every .css under apps/control-room/src. That was true when written and is FALSE NOW — verified by me at 15:43Z:
  apps/control-room/src/shell/shell-layout.css:35  transition: inline-size 160ms ease;
  apps/control-room/src/shell/shell-layout.css:58  transition: transform 160ms ease;

BUT THE ACCESSIBILITY PROPERTY IS ACTUALLY HONOURED, which is why the DoD is wrong rather than the code:
  shell-layout.css:131  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  shell-layout.css:136    animation: none;
  shell-layout.css:138    transition: none;
And the same gate exists in approvals/approval-layout.css:34, board/board-layout.css:68 and styles/responsive.css:151.

So motion EXISTS and is correctly SUPPRESSED for users who ask for that. A guard banning motion outright would forbid legitimate, accessible UI and would have to be either weakened or deleted the moment anyone adds a transition — the exact "guard that rots into false evidence" failure epic rail 6 exists to prevent.

CORRECTED DoD ITEM 1: assert that EVERY motion declaration in apps/control-room/src/**/*.css is overridden to none within a @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) block in the same stylesheet. Assert the sweep found a NON-ZERO number of motion declarations before asserting they are all gated — a sweep that silently matches nothing must not pass, per epic rail 6. A stylesheet that introduces motion without its own reduced-motion block fails, which is the property worth guarding and it is stable as the UI grows.

ITEMS 2-6 ARE UNAFFECTED and were already ready per the architect's own assessment.

I cannot edit definitionOfDone — no MCP tool exposes it and this task has no plan steps to amend — so this reason field is the durable record and QA inherits it. FOR QA: a diff satisfying item 1 by BANNING motion, or by deleting/weakening the guard, is a rejection. The guard must prove motion is gated, not absent.
